{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/format.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952270Z","id":"56483089c45c67c032c9f840615a70d73124a6bf7eaaea1b79bc6da39da15204","body":{"detail":"Failure: a hand-written annotation line with a custom body field, e.g. body {\"kind\":\"concern\",\"score\":-10,\"summary\":\"hand\"}, loses `score` when the file is rewritten by `qualifier compact <artifact>` (any prune that rewrites the file); `qualifier emit annotation a.txt --body '{\"kind\":\"concern\",\"summary\":\"x\",\"score\":-10}'` also writes the record without `score`. Reproduced with qualifier 0.8.0 in a scratch git repo. Cause: `AnnotationBody` in src/annotation.rs:245-262 has no `#[serde(flatten)]` catch-all, so serde drops unknown keys on parse, and `compact` re-serializes the struct via `qual_file::write_all`. The stored `id` is kept, so after compaction the record's ID no longer matches its content. This contradicts site/pages/format.md:156-163 ('Records that round-trip through tooling preserve unknown body fields verbatim'), SPEC.md §4.1 (tools MAY add a `score` body field) and SPEC.md §6.5 ('The body is passed through unchanged'). The whole SPEC §4 layering story depends on custom body fields surviving the reference CLI.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"80af188a83d1ed485363f2d9b2246e8c40c725576fd93bf1f5e22788f53c7b96"},"suggested_fix":"Add `#[serde(flatten)] pub extra: serde_json::Map<String, serde_json::Value>` (or a BTreeMap) to AnnotationBody and EpochBody so unknown keys round-trip and participate in MCF hashing in sorted position; add a regression in tests/cli_integration.rs that compacts a file containing a custom body field and asserts the field and ID survive. Until fixed, remove the preservation claim from format.md and SPEC §6.5.","summary":"Docs promise unknown annotation body fields are preserved verbatim, but emit and compact silently strip them","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:18:11.952610Z","id":"5e50b2b4870baa81b22e33faead9900c4291a9f837d10da2a47123666996a43b","body":{"detail":"site/pages/cli.md 'Commands' lists only record/reply/resolve/emit/show/ls/praise/review/compact; `threads` (0.8.0), `diff`, `init` and `agents` are absent, though `qualifier --help` lists them. Line 48 says 'All commands that produce output accept --format json', but `compact` rejects `--format` ('unexpected argument'). Line 135 says 'For `--type annotation`, the body is validated' but emit takes the type as the first positional; there is no `--type` flag on emit (src/cli/commands/emit.rs Args). Line 127 emits a license with body `{\"spdx\":\"MIT\"}`, while SPEC.md §3.5 names the required field `spdx_id`. SPEC.md §6.5 (lines 1095-1100) has the same `--type annotation` wording and `spdx` example.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"0dd4b4524e91a10e9811e42d380a91ee90ce23ecef2102eb2d9557be8e0752c9"},"suggested_fix":"Add threads, diff, init and agents to the command blocks; say 'read commands accept --format json'; replace '--type annotation' with 'when <type> is annotation' in both cli.md and SPEC §6.5; change both license examples to `{\"spdx_id\":\"MIT\"}`.","summary":"Site CLI page is missing threads, diff, init and agents, and its examples use flags and fields that do not exist","tags":["review","review:2026-10-01","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/format.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611211Z","id":"3706760a8a19483998c100a49b8156c4ed62e57a706149e82ebc724cbcaab4fa","body":{"detail":"src/annotation.rs:245-262 AnnotationBody has no #[serde(flatten)] catch-all. Scratch git repo, qualifier 0.8.0: `qualifier emit annotation a.txt --body '{\"kind\":\"concern\",\"summary\":\"x\",\"score\":-10}'` wrote body {\"kind\":\"concern\",\"summary\":\"x\"}. Hand-added \"score\":-10 to another record's body, resolved a third record, then `qualifier compact a.txt` printed '3 -> 2 records (1 superseded, pruned)' and `grep -c score .qual` went 1 -> 0; the surviving record kept its stored id a95ec999... though its content changed. site/pages/format.md:162-163 and SPEC.md:1092-1093 promise verbatim pass-through.","kind":"comment","references":"56483089c45c67c032c9f840615a70d73124a6bf7eaaea1b79bc6da39da15204","summary":"confirmed: emit and compact drop unknown annotation body fields, contradicting format.md's preservation promise","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:21:38.611287Z","id":"2890faddd16ad2ceab41f1934536f24ccb5cb85d2bd6158f5db09819f6c1e776","body":{"detail":"site/pages/cli.md:17-46 command blocks have no threads, diff, init, or agents. Line 48 claims all output commands take --format json; `qualifier compact src/lib.rs --format json --dry-run` -> \"error: unexpected argument '--format' found\". src/cli/commands/emit.rs:11-15 takes the type as a positional (no --type flag), yet cli.md:135 and SPEC.md:1093-1095 say 'For --type annotation'. cli.md:127 and SPEC.md:1099 use body {\"spdx\":\"MIT\"} while SPEC.md:670 names the required field spdx_id.","kind":"comment","references":"5e50b2b4870baa81b22e33faead9900c4291a9f837d10da2a47123666996a43b","summary":"confirmed: site CLI page omits threads/diff/init/agents and its --format, --type, and spdx examples are wrong","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/cli.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212713Z","id":"33c46ac3e7b43197d7524f9e3273b984713686bb3516efcf223d95338a16a2e9","body":{"detail":"Evidence: site/pages/cli.md:127 `--body '{\"spdx\":\"MIT\"}'` vs SPEC.md:670 required field spdx_id; `qualifier compact <f> --format json` -> unexpected argument","kind":"comment","references":"5e50b2b4870baa81b22e33faead9900c4291a9f837d10da2a47123666996a43b","summary":"Resolution: In site/pages/cli.md: add threads, diff, init, and agents to the command blocks (17-46); at line 48 say 'read commands accept --format json'; at line 135 (and SPEC.md:1093-1095) replace '--type annotation' with 'when <type> is annotation'; at line 127 (and SPEC.md:1099) change the body to {\"spdx_id\":\"MIT\"}.","tags":["session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"site/pages/format.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-01T20:33:23.212862Z","id":"1c2bcadcaee4a5c67ee215496df26b9e3b249de9c1e8f0c6148cc39b411dcbb6","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Duplicate of b913d1d1782800e4de9bbc9f86d08f09728ec08674a605de4bee413c4b106a42, which makes the same claim with the same root cause; follow that thread.","supersedes":"56483089c45c67c032c9f840615a70d73124a6bf7eaaea1b79bc6da39da15204","tags":["reason:duplicate","session:claude-code:906ddd45-2dc1-4a64-9674-56eec33bd6f1"]}}
